<<~ ahu slot=`#/numerical-lineage`>>

!! The numerical path's lineage

The text the api meme's #/the-numerical-path carried before the ever-speaking-present cure, kept verbatim:

> ''This path stands partly ENACTED, not only designed.'' The sensorium's `settlePrecision` already carries the closed-form settle and the complementary-form guard against the large-ε̄² divergence (commit lineage `f50a35b8` //sensorium.numerics.harden — signal-fraction confidence · closed-form settle · complementary π→conf//; the QA hardening in `ab85fc2b` caught the large-ε̄² divergence and the false-critical / EWS-guard leaks). That enactment lives ''py/R'' — the full sensorium model's home, instanced per-stream — while TS keeps the pure-functor math floor these identities also seed. The record honors the enacted-vs-aimed cut: the numerical path stands in code py/R-side, where the sensorium reads; the fusion escape and the structure descent stand as design grounded in established algorithms not yet all wired.

The grounds line carried the same lineage: "ENACTED py/R-side in the sensorium `settlePrecision` (commits `f50a35b8`, `ab85fc2b`, `f9d07e49`) — signal-fraction confidence, closed-form settle, complementary π→conf guard; TS keeps the pure-functor math floor these identities seed."

At the cure, `settlePrecision` reads in TypeScript at `packages/lararium-mesh/src/sensorium-pc.ts`; the py/R home the old text named no longer carries it.

<<~/ahu>>

